; With --download, prefetch_quotes() fetches a commodity whose only price
; comes from a P directive in the batch call.  It used to read the
; inverted price of "$" (priced in AAPL by the same P line) as an
; exchange, drop AAPL as "an exchange commodity", and fetch nothing.
; The mock script answers only --batch, so a missed prefetch shows as a
; warning and the stale $100 price.

P 2024/01/01 AAPL $100.00

2024/01/15 Opening balance
    Assets:Brokerage        10 AAPL
    Equity:Opening

test bal Assets:Brokerage --market --now 2030/06/15 --download --getquote $sourcepath/test/scripts/mock-getquote-batch-only.sh
            $1500.00  Assets:Brokerage
end test

test pricedb --now 2030/06/15 --download --getquote $sourcepath/test/scripts/mock-getquote-batch-only.sh
P 2024/01/01 00:00:00 AAPL $100.00
P 2024/06/15 00:00:00 AAPL $150.00
end test
